<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 19 April, from 531 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belisarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">531 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Persians defeat Belisarius at the Battle of Callinicum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Iberian War, a Sasanian Persian army defeated the Byzantine army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> at Callinicum (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raqqa">Raqqa</a>), in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, on Easter Saturday. Belisarius had beaten the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> at Dara in 530.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1042">1042 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">984 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A popular revolt in Constantinople restores Empress Zoe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When Emperor Michael V Kalaphates tried to sideline his adoptive mother, Empress Zoe Porphyrogenita, a popular revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> forced him to restore her, together with her sister Theodora. Michael was deposed the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1506">1506 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A massacre of New Christians begins in Lisbon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A crowd of churchgoers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> attacked and killed several people in the congregation whom they suspected of being <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. The violence grew into a city-wide riot that killed between 500 and 4,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a>, Jews who had been forcibly converted.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1529">1529 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lutheran princes protest at the Diet of Speyer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six princes and fourteen imperial cities formally protested against the Diet's move to curb the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. Their Protestation gave the movement the name 'Protestant'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1713">1713 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">313 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Charles VI issues the Pragmatic Sanction</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Charles VI, who had no living male heirs, issued an edict ensuring that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy could be inherited undivided by a daughter. He later spent years winning acceptance of the Pragmatic Sanction for his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-holy-roman-emperor">Charles VI</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Shots at Lexington and Concord begin the American Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Militiamen clashed with British regulars at Lexington and Concord in Massachusetts, and harried them all the way back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>. The skirmishes began the War of Independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1897">1897 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">129 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Boston Marathon is run</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Fifteen</a> runners set out on the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> race, inspired by the marathon at the 1896 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> Olympics. It is now the world's oldest annual marathon.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Warsaw Ghetto Uprising begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jewish fighters resisted German troops sent to deport the ghetto's remaining inhabitants to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treblinka-extermination-camp">Treblinka</a>. They held out for nearly a month in the largest Jewish revolt of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1995">1995 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truck bomb kills 168 in Oklahoma City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Timothy McVeigh detonated a truck bomb outside the Alfred P. Murrah Federal Building, killing 168 people, including 19 children. It remains the deadliest act of domestic terrorism in US history.</p></div></li></ol>
